The supplied semantics already models the key operations needed here: string iteration, `startswith`, slicing, and function frames. I’m choosing a source implementation that scans every suffix one character at a time; this makes overlap explicit and gives the proof a structural invariant over the unscanned suffix. The empty-substring case is handled separately so the function agrees with Python’s `n + 1` boundary behavior.
