codex
The lemma-free variant does not close: the backend will not unfold the recursive summary at the needed symbolic shape, and forcing it causes recursive simplification. I’ve restored the audited slice-to-tail lemma; this is exactly the kind of narrow, derived mathematical fact the Kit permits when the fixed evaluator cannot normalize a symbolic operation. Its guard and context are universal over every nonempty `IntSeq`, and it has no control or state footprint.
exec
/bin/bash -lc './prove.sh >/tmp/how-many-times-prove.log 2>&1
tail -n 30 /tmp/how-many-times-prove.log' in /workspace
